<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arevaci</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Arevaci were the most powerful Celtiberian people, living in the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douro">Douro</a> valley around the modern province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soria">Soria</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. Their towns included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/numantia">Numantia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiermes">Termes</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uxama-argaela">Uxama</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clunia">Clunia</a>. They led the resistance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in the Celtiberian Wars and especially the Numantine War of 143–133 BCE, which ended with the destruction of Numantia by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scipio-aemilianus">Scipio Aemilianus</a>.</p></div>
